{"created": "2025-02-15T13:32:14.410883+00:00", "modified": "2025-09-09T14:48:44.560716+00:00", "id": 14875701, "conceptrecid": "14272279", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14875701", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.14272279", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14875701", "metadata": {"title": "Machine Proofs for Adams Differentials and Extension Problems among CW Spectra", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14875701", "publication_date": "2025-02-15", "description": "<p>Update notes: In this version, we reduce the number of spectra in this project from 210 to 49 (compared to the cw210 version), while keeping the outcome sufficient to prove <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.10879\">the Last Kervaire Invariant Problem</a>. The size of the proof file <a href=\"https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875532/draft/files/proofs.db.rar/content\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">proofs.db.rar</a> is also reduced from 600MB to 44MB, leading to easier track for proofs.</p>\n<p>In this Zenodo repository we upload the computations of Adams differentials and extensions among many CW spectra and their proofs. This data will be used in the <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.10879\">proof of the Last Kervaire Invariant Problem</a> by Weinan Lin, Guozhen Wang and Zhouli Xu.</p>\n<p>In <strong>programs.rar</strong>, we have two programs ./Adams and ./ss provided for both windows users and mac users and a definition file <strong>Adams.json</strong> for spectra involved in this project.&nbsp;The source code for the two programs is contained in <strong>source code.zip</strong>. You can also find the source code on Github <a href=\"https://github.com/WayneLin92/SSeqCpp\">https://github.com/WayneLin92/SSeqCpp</a> together with user manual for the programs.</p>\n<p>In <strong>programs.rar</strong> there is also a demo for ./ss which is a category of five spectra: S0, C2, Ceta, Cnu, Csigma.</p>\n<p><strong>kervaire_database.rar</strong> contains all the Adams spectral sequence data and extension data. They are sqlite3 database files and can be read directly by the ./ss program. We also provide the same data in csv format in <strong>kervaire_csv.rar</strong>.</p>\n<p>The two zip files<strong> proofs.db.rar</strong> and <strong>proofs_csv.rar</strong> are proofs of all the differentials. Inside <strong>proofs_csv.rar</strong> there are 3 csv files. We break it to 3 csv files because Microsoft Excel has a limit of 1,000,000 rows.</p>\n<p>On the website <a href=\"https://waynelin92.github.io/ss/kervaire-49.html\">https://waynelin92.github.io/ss/kervaire-49.html</a> you can find plots of the data. The website source code (html/javascript) is actually contained in&nbsp;<strong>programs.rar</strong>/webpages in this repository.</p>\n<p>Please read <strong>instructions.pdf</strong> for more infomation.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Lin, Weinan", "affiliation": "Fudan University", "orcid": "0000-0002-0398-7643"}, {"name": "Wang, Guozhen", "affiliation": "Fudan University"}, {"name": "Xu, Zhouli", "affiliation": "University of California, Los Angeles"}], "keywords": ["Stable homotopy theory", "Kervaire invariant"], "version": "v126.3.cw49", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/WayneLin92/SSeqCpp", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "c++", "title": {"en": "C++"}}, {"id": "javascript", "title": {"en": "JavaScript"}}, {"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}, {"id": "sql", "title": {"en": "SQL"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 4, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "14272279"}}]}}, "title": "Machine Proofs for Adams Differentials and Extension Problems among CW Spectra", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/14875701", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/14875701?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14875701", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14875701", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.14875701", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14272279", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/14272279", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14272279", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.14272279", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701:instructions.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701:instructions.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701:instructions.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701:instructions.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701:instructions.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:14875701:instructions.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/14875701/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/14875701/commu